       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high. At that level there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg is a typo. Here are some options:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily** is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily** is the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily** is a lower starting dose, sometimes used for frail or elderly patients.\n\nIf you tell me the dose you want, I'll enter it right away. If you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding a second agent from a different class is the usual approach. That decision should go through the prescriber and pharmacy."
